[h1]1.0[/h1]

0.9.x was the trading systems; 1.0 is the world those systems trade in. Settlements now have economies that differ, drift and recover, and a reputation you build inside them.

[hr][/hr]
[h1]Settlements[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Settlements differ in what they produce, need and can supply.[/b] Their economies are different enough that where you trade matters.
[*][b]Shortages and surpluses persist long enough to plan around.[/b] They drift over time and then normalise, instead of being replaced by unrelated market noise every refresh.
[*][b]Economic events can create a temporary need or supply.[/b] A circumstance somewhere is worth trading into while it lasts.
[/list]

[h1]Your reputation[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Quality goods build brand strength per product family.[/b] It affects price and interest, and a colony known for one kind of work is not automatically known for everything.
[/list]

[h1]Negotiation[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Important offers can be countered within bounded rules.[/b] The counter is constrained rather than open-ended.
[*][b]If a deal you already accepted becomes hard to meet you can ask for a constrained renegotiation.[/b] The original obligation stays in force until the new terms are actually accepted, so asking is not an escape hatch.
[/list]

[h1]Buying[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Procurement is now as complete as selling.[/b] Search the supplier market, collect and compare quotations, place purchase orders, and set up standing procurement agreements when a one-off purchase is not enough.
[/list]

[h1]Relations[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Each settlement keeps the commercial history of your dealings with it in one place.[/b] That history includes completed and failed work, purchases, agreements, renegotiations and brand milestones.
[/list]

[h1]Saves[/h1]

[b]The save format DID change.[/b] Existing colonies migrate from schema 42 up to schema 56 on load. No existing obligation changes its price or its quantity across that migration — that is asserted by the test suite, not hoped.

Keep a backup of any colony you care about before loading it with this update, same as always.

1.0 is no longer a beta. Problems to the [url=https://github.com/miannoni/Intercolony/issues]GitHub issue tracker[/url], please, with your mod list and [b]Player.log[/b].
